Z||000004||Old Lar||10-12-2001||08:13 AM||||The only car to beat the Fiero in crash tests was the Volvo when they were tested in the 80's.<P>As for kiddie seats, I almost think it would be easier to have a Fiero seat specially set for the child seat, then remove the four bolts take the stock Fiero seat out, and reinstall the specialty kiddy seat.  Installing the belt in seats is a pain.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Congrats on the next generation Fiero driver.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Little Duce Coupe||10-12-2001||01:53 PM||||Hey Congratulations!<P>We have a two year old and a fiero also (duh).<BR>One word of caution though. Be very particular with the baby seat you choose.  We had purchased two seats one for our Explorer and the other for the inlaws van, the thought was that I would take one or the other when I needed it for the Fiero.<BR>It didn't work that way though.<BR>The combination of a low seat bottom and a tall seat belt receiver meant I could never get the seat to snug down like their supposed to.  <BR>If you find a good one that works please post, we have another on the way and I never did find a seat for my "Little Coupe".<BR><P>------------------<BR>Little Duce Coupe<BR>"You Don't Know What She Costs"||||reg||4
Z||000006||Brian87egotrip||10-12-2001||05:06 PM||||Congrats.  I just had my baby 3 weeks ago. Haven't even tried a baby seat in it yet. If you figure something out let me know.  <P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||jfuredy||10-12-2001||06:52 PM||||I have a 10 month old daughter (very cute, BTW) and I have a car seat in my Fiero.  Before she was born I went to a 2-hour class on car seat safety.  They told us all about how to install the seats and the different types of seat belts.<P>You CANNOT SAFELY put a car seat in a Fiero with the stock seat belts.  Most shoulder belts are anchored at one, has an inertia reel on the other end and the latch slides on the belt to adjust.  The Fiero's belt has inertia reels on BOTH ENDS with the latch at a fixed point.  That is the reason that Little Duce Coupe couldn't get the belt cinched down.<P>What I did to solve this problem was install a simple lap belt from the middle rear seat of a 1992 Ford Tempo using the stock Fiero mounting points.  So now I have two belts installed: the stock shoulder belt, and the lap belt for the car seat.<P>Sorry this got so long, but child safety is about as important of a topic as I can think of.  Let me know if you have any questions.<P>Joe Furedy<BR>'88 Formula<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dumba$$||10-12-2001||10:11 PM||||the car seat that we have is from Grayco<BR>the base of it stays in the car and the seat clips right in, which is nice cuz then you dont have to disturb the kid!! it works really well in our acura, actually better than i thought biengs its only a 2 door.  I think the base concept would suck in a fiero because the base is made to pretty much stay in the car so i think well find somthing else for the fiero<BR>thanks guys<BR>||||reg||1
